{
  "note": "What ../pipeline/capture.mjs records off a booted emulator, for app 1.0.3. Coordinates are for a 1080 x 2400 screen at 420 dpi, which is what `./run.sh --emulator` boots; a screenshot is 1:1 with input taps, so `node ../pipeline/capture.mjs --probe` is how to re-read them when a screen moves. `setup` runs before the recorder starts, `steps` run while it is rolling, `teardown` runs after it has stopped. Nothing is cropped downstream any more — every beat shows the whole screen inside a phone frame — so a shot only has to be framed for time, not for which band of the screen it lands in.",
  "order": "Shots that change the project come after the ones that read it, and `pick` is last because it makes a second project. `saving` writes an export into the gallery, so `../pipeline/pull-export.mjs` runs after it and the export is deleted from the gallery before `pick` — otherwise the picker's first tile is a video that already has captions burned into it.",
